From c908bdb80b3add55369009f98ba5e39476ebc53a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] vkr: import shm resources as host memory, log failed
 allocations

On a host that emulates dma_buf on top of VK_EXT_external_memory_host
(macOS/MoltenVK), every resource the guest sees as a dma_buf is POSIX shm
(VIRGL_RESOURCE_FD_SHM).  Importing one into a VkDeviceMemory with
VkImportMemoryResourceInfoMESA failed with VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE,
silently with async allocation, and the guest's next use of the memory
(e.g. vkBindImageMemory2 from zink importing a glamor dma_buf) hit
"failed to look up object" and killed the ring.

vkr_resource now keeps the shm fd of shm resources, whether imported, created
as shm or exported from a VkDeviceMemory.  The latter also gets the mapping
every shm resource is expected to carry in u.data; it used to store the fd in
u.fd and munmap() it as a pointer on destruction.

vkAllocateMemory maps the shm (MAP_SHARED, own mapping, size rounded up to
the page size and minImportedHostPointerAlignment) and imports the mapping
with VkImportMemoryHostPointerInfoEXT, choosing a memory type the host
pointer supports if the requested one is not.  The mapping lives in
mem->shm, so exporting the memory again hands out the same shm, and it is
released on vkFreeMemory.  vkGetMemoryResourcePropertiesMESA reports the
host pointer memory types for shm resources.

vkAllocateMemory failures are logged with VkResult, size, memory type,
import kind and export handle types.
